<article class="env-lemma" id="0DRI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DRI">Lemma <span data-tag="0DRI">107.5.4</span>.</a> If $f: U \to X$ is a smooth morphism of locally Noetherian algebraic spaces, and if $u \in |U|$ with image $x \in |X|$, then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _ u (U) = \dim _ x(X) + \dim _{u} (U_ x)  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\dim _ u (U_ x)$ is defined via Definition <a href="/tag/0DRG" data-tag="0DRG">107.5.2</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      See Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AFI" data-tag="0AFI">67.37.10</a> noting that the definition of $\dim _ u (U_ x)$ used here coincides with the definition used there, by Remark <a href="/tag/0DRH" data-tag="0DRH">107.5.3</a> (2). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>